{"text": " You don't need more free time to read 12 books a year. You need 10 pages a night. Most of us wait for a quiet weekend to read. It never really comes, so the book sits on the nightstand with the bookmark stuck on page 40. Do the math instead. 10 pages takes about 15 minutes. 10 pages every night is 3,650 pages a year. At 300 pages a book, that's 12 books. Here's the method. Put the book on your pillow in the morning. At night, 10 pages first before you touch your phone, then the phone. And track pages, not books. 12 books feels far away. 10 pages is something you finish tonight. Pick tonight's book right now and put it on your pillow before dinner. That's what Demure is for. You archive your dream today so you can see it tomorrow and break it down into small steps you can actually do. If you want to try it out, I've put the link in the bio.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 5.34, "text": " You don't need more free time to read 12 books a year. You need 10 pages a night. Most of us wait", "tokens": [50363, 921, 836, 470, 761, 517, 1479, 640, 284, 1100, 1105, 3835, 257, 614, 13, 921, 761, 838, 5468, 257, 1755, 13, 4042, 286, 514, 4043, 50627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08169139058966386, "compression_ratio": 1.7402135231316727, "no_speech_prob": 0.0013001671759411693, "words": [{"word": " You", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.24, "probability": 0.621173620223999}, {"word": " don't", "start": 0.24, "end": 0.38, "probability": 0.9796730577945709}, {"word": " need", "start": 0.38, "end": 0.54, "probability": 0.998855710029602}, {"word": " more", "start": 0.54, "end": 0.76, "probability": 0.9965890645980835}, {"word": " free", "start": 0.76, "end": 0.98, "probability": 0.9948950409889221}, {"word": " time", "start": 0.98, "end": 1.24, "probability": 0.9913399815559387}, {"word": " to", "start": 1.24, "end": 1.42, "probability": 0.9964589476585388}, {"word": " read", "start": 1.42, "end": 1.58, "probability": 0.9980964064598083}, {"word"